# macro_type_splice.tkr — the §14 A4 ACCEPT host: `@Type()` in a TYPE position (the §9.D inline-union
# abbreviation). Each scenario names itself and asserts its announced value through `run` in `main.tks`.
# A `@macro()` in a field/slice type re-parses its `lowering` fragment as a TypeExpr, spliced pre-type-
# check: `@Elem()` -> i64, `@NumOrStr()` -> the inline union `i64 | str`, `[]@Elem()` -> `[]i64`.

Feature: macro_type_splice — @Type() type-position splice (§14 A4 / §9.D)

  Scenario: macro_type_elem — a field type @Elem() expands to i64
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario macro_type_elem: ok"

  Scenario: macro_type_union — @NumOrStr() expands to the inline union i64 | str (§9.D keystone)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario macro_type_union: ok"

  Scenario: macro_type_slice — []@Elem() expands to the slice type []i64
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario macro_type_slice: ok"
